    "created_at": "2016-07-30T14:20:20Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-07-30T14:20:20Z",
    "body": "```\n/^[a-zA-Z0-9.!#$%&'*+\\/=?^_`{|}~-]+@[a-zA-Z0-9](?:[a-zA-Z0-9-]{0,61}[a-zA-Z0-9])?(?:\\.[a-zA-Z0-9](?:[a-zA-Z0-9-]{0,61}[a-zA-Z0-9])?)*$/.test(\"foo@bar.rocks\")\n\n>> true\n```\n\nThis regex (and the grammar which it is based on; the regex is non-normative) handle new TLDs just fine. In fact they handle basically any 63-or-less character string after the . sign.\n\nClosing since I believe there is no bug here, but happy to continue discussing in the closed thread if there is still some confusion.\n",
